From 87323a76f8e2aa75524482a6f2668673fc174ad9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:00:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: drop the always-zero glyph count from the outlying rune
 score

When borg_flow_glyph() extends an existing Sea of Runes it scores each
unglyphed grid of the 5x5 block around the stored centre as
500 + (tmp_glyph * 500) - cost.  tmp_glyph is only counted in the
new-sea branch, so in this branch it is always 0 and the score is
500 - cost: the borg glyphs the nearest unglyphed grid next.

Write the score as 500 - cost.  No behaviour change; it only makes the
nearest-first choice explicit.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#115.
---
 src/borg/borg-flow-glyph.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-flow-glyph.c b/src/borg/borg-flow-glyph.c
index 5af26cf95..5f349a80e 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-flow-glyph.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-flow-glyph.c
@@ -250,7 +250,7 @@ bool borg_flow_glyph(void)
                         continue;
 
                     /* Tweak -- Reward certain floors, punish distance */
-                    v = 500 + (tmp_glyph * 500) - (cost * 1);
+                    v = 500 - (cost * 1);
 
                     /* The grid is not searchable */
                     if (v <= 0)
-- 
